(5641044, 817974, 88136, '<td valign="top">omg this is frickin beautiful! it seriously feels like im looking at a real flower in front of my laptop. its so soft, the way that petals are soft and kinda squishy. truely amazing, very big congrats on the fs blue:)</td>', 'omg this is frickin beautiful! it seriously feels like im looking at a real flower in front of my laptop. its so soft, the way that petals are soft and kinda squishy. truely amazing, very big congrats on the fs blue:)', '2009-09-08 23:02:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(5641074, 817276, 61818, '<td valign="top">The most interesting parts of the photo (one of which you even highlight in your comments - the bridge) are diminished by the overwhelming presence of water and sky.  This makes it very hard to find a point of interest to focus on, and the eyes just wander around in vain until the mind just stops caring.  My suggestion would be to frame it (or crop it) so that the boat and bridge are much more prominent in the frame.  720 pixels don''t go a long way, gotta make the most of them.</td>', 'The most interesting parts of the photo (one of which you even highlight in your comments - the bridge) are diminished by the overwhelming presence of water and sky.  This makes it very hard to find a point of interest to focus on, and the eyes just wander around in vain until the mind just stops caring.  My suggestion would be to frame it (or crop it) so that the boat and bridge are much more prominent in the frame.  720 pixels don''t go a long way, gotta make the most of them.', '2009-09-08 23:21:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(5641097, 816045, 53814, '<td valign="top">you need this lens :)</td>', 'you need this lens :)', '2009-09-08 23:43:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5641105, 817917, 86447, '<td valign="top">I feel like I''m in Oz.<br/> <br/>There''s no place like home... There''s no place like home...</td>', 'I feel like I''m in Oz. There''s no place like home... There''s no place like home...', '2009-09-08 23:54:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5641117, 815450, 23027, '<td valign="top">Awesome in so many ways.  Congratulations on this wonderful memory you and your Aunt Kate captured.</td>', 'Awesome in so many ways.  Congratulations on this wonderful memory you and your Aunt Kate captured.', '2009-09-09 00:06:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5641126, 818441, 34547, '<td valign="top">bspurgeon, thanks for the great feedback.  I have to confess that I''m still prone to shooting rapidly and without too much planning. This photo was one of numerous in a span of 5 minutes where I was trying to do panoramas and different angles, etc.  The downside is that I could have framed the photo better and spent the time to adjust the camera for a good exposure in the ways you have commented.  With the HDR, this is still very much an experiment. I had problems with the mountain having very strange, blown out looking highlights with the tone mapping and after your comment I can see that the sunny side is a bit overdone.  I just loved the colors so much and wanted it to burst.  Thanks again for the detailed comments.  You can find that B&amp;B here: <a href="//www.northcountrybnb.com/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">North Country B&amp;B, Trapper Creek, AK</a></td>', 'bspurgeon, thanks for the great feedback.  I have to confess that I''m still prone to shooting rapidly and without too much planning. This photo was one of numerous in a span of 5 minutes where I was trying to do panoramas and different angles, etc.  The downside is that I could have framed the photo better and spent the time to adjust the camera for a good exposure in the ways you have commented.  With the HDR, this is still very much an experiment. I had problems with the mountain having very strange, blown out looking highlights with the tone mapping and after your comment I can see that the sunny side is a bit overdone.  I just loved the colors so much and wanted it to burst.  Thanks again for the detailed comments.  You can find that B&B here: North Country B&B, Trapper Creek, AK', '2009-09-09 00:13:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5641167, 815450, 5034, '<td valign="top">You accomplished your goal in having a photo you can frame.  It is simply stunning.  You could probably make a packet from this one.  I know it''s crushing to get this close - heck, you made the grade - and then have it taken away.  But you know you can do it.</td>', 'You accomplished your goal in having a photo you can frame.  It is simply stunning.  You could probably make a packet from this one.  I know it''s crushing to get this close - heck, you made the grade - and then have it taken away.  But you know you can do it.', '2009-09-09 00:42:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5641175, 817974, 60862, '<td valign="top">Wow, what a roll!  This is just a gorgeous, gorgeous shot.  Just an amazing image of a flower, and we''ve all seen plenty of flowers!  Congrats!</td>', 'Wow, what a roll!  This is just a gorgeous, gorgeous shot.  Just an amazing image of a flower, and we''ve all seen plenty of flowers!  Congrats!', '2009-09-09 00:48:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5641232, 814329, 30982, '<td valign="top">Holy cow, Andi!  Congrats!!</td>', 'Holy cow, Andi!  Congrats!!', '2009-09-09 01:11:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5641361, 817974, 6845, '<td valign="top">Wow Anna, awesome, awesome!!</td>', 'Wow Anna, awesome, awesome!!', '2009-09-09 02:27:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5641368, 817866, 1031, '<td valign="top">Shallow DOF is fine by me, and those eyes are very bright!<br/> <br/>Since you say he wasn''t moving around, you could have tried taking multiple images with different focal planes, and then combining them in post processing to artificially increase the DOF. I''ve never done it, but it is one if the uses of multiple images specifically allowed under the Advanced Rules.<br/> <br/>Still, I think those bright eyes helped get you the extra 3/4 point you scored over my bumblebee. ;-)</td>', 'Shallow DOF is fine by me, and those eyes are very bright! Since you say he wasn''t moving around, you could have tried taking multiple images with different focal planes, and then combining them in post processing to artificially increase the DOF. I''ve never done it, but it is one if the uses of multiple images specifically allowed under the Advanced Rules. Still, I think those bright eyes helped get you the extra 3/4 point you scored over my bumblebee. ;-)', '2009-09-09 02:37:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(5641386, 815450, 106806, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mm767cap:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ineedauniquename:</b></div><hr/><i> any chance of seeing the original 5 before combining, this HDR lark is driving me nuts a bit and it would be interesting to see the starting material. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually, it''s not an HDR image.  I manually blended the 5 exposures.  </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Did you mask bits out of different layers?</td>', 'Originally posted by mm767cap: Originally posted by ineedauniquename: any chance of seeing the original 5 before combining, this HDR lark is driving me nuts a bit and it would be interesting to see the starting material.   Actually, it''s not an HDR image.  I manually blended the 5 exposures.    Did you mask bits out of different layers?', '2009-09-09 02:53:00.000000', NULL, 0),
