(5647073, 814069, 65234, '<td valign="top">First time I saw one of these guys I was completely confused as to what sort of Heron it was.  I''d only seen the adults before.  I don''t know why birds insist on changing appearance when growing up AND/or growing amorous; it''s much harder to ID them in anything other than adult breeding plumage!<br/> <br/>Nice detail and I like how he has his feet positioned; looks kind of endearingly awkward.</td>', 'First time I saw one of these guys I was completely confused as to what sort of Heron it was.  I''d only seen the adults before.  I don''t know why birds insist on changing appearance when growing up AND/or growing amorous; it''s much harder to ID them in anything other than adult breeding plumage! Nice detail and I like how he has his feet positioned; looks kind of endearingly awkward.', '2009-09-14 19:42:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5647081, 818268, 18450, '<td valign="top">I think this is one of the most beautiful portraits I''ve seen. Stunning shot!</td>', 'I think this is one of the most beautiful portraits I''ve seen. Stunning shot!', '2009-09-14 19:48:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(5647167, 818267, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: Yummy! :-) Unusual subject matter, but compelling the more you look at it.  Good use of Topaz, because it''s evident you used it, but not over-done.<br/> <br/>Technical: Nicely done use of thirds.  Looks very vivid especially for an overhead shot, which usually risks looking flat.<br/> <br/>Artistic: I find the eye a little creepy, which is good, as is the frozen-open mouth and nasty pointy teeth.<br/> <br/>Overall: Good work! Pity it didn''t score higher, but Free Studies are always tough.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: Yummy! :-) Unusual subject matter, but compelling the more you look at it.  Good use of Topaz, because it''s evident you used it, but not over-done. Technical: Nicely done use of thirds.  Looks very vivid especially for an overhead shot, which usually risks looking flat. Artistic: I find the eye a little creepy, which is good, as is the frozen-open mouth and nasty pointy teeth. Overall: Good work! Pity it didn''t score higher, but Free Studies are always tough. Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-09-14 21:28:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5647221, 818294, 59029, '<td valign="top">Wow.<br/> <br/>uh, oh yeah, Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: stunning image, looks like an opening shot for a scene from Lord of the Rings trilogy.<br/> <br/>Technical:  If you look for it, you can see the editing.  But if you''re not, well, it just comes off as a lovely shot with tons of depth and lines leading you in deeper...and deeper...into the shot.  Love pix like this.<br/> <br/>Artistic: *scratching head* what can I say that hasn''t already been said?  Gorgeous use of ambient light, if not for the small traces of humanity visible at the base of these towering mountains, I''d think I really was on my way to Mordor or some other fantastical place.<br/> <br/>Overall: Uhmm....as in how to improve this picture?  I can''t think of any way to do so.  It truly is gorgeous.  May be a bit discouraging to have finished on a 5.7, but remember it''s a Free Study.  So in almost any other challenge it would likely have easily finished in the 6s.<br/> <br/>Great work, keep it up!<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Wow. uh, oh yeah, Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: stunning image, looks like an opening shot for a scene from Lord of the Rings trilogy. Technical:  If you look for it, you can see the editing.  But if you''re not, well, it just comes off as a lovely shot with tons of depth and lines leading you in deeper...and deeper...into the shot.  Love pix like this. Artistic: *scratching head* what can I say that hasn''t already been said?  Gorgeous use of ambient light, if not for the small traces of humanity visible at the base of these towering mountains, I''d think I really was on my way to Mordor or some other fantastical place. Overall: Uhmm....as in how to improve this picture?  I can''t think of any way to do so.  It truly is gorgeous.  May be a bit discouraging to have finished on a 5.7, but remember it''s a Free Study.  So in almost any other challenge it would likely have easily finished in the 6s. Great work, keep it up! Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-09-14 22:14:06.000000', NULL, 0),
