(5714463, 817623, 67145, '<td valign="top">hey sandy .. just came visiting and clicked on this awesome photograph .... its totally beautiful .. it looks fine on my pc but i like the darkness and the really rich orange/red of the sand .. its like a surfer has come out''v the water at the end of the day as darkness approaches .. the water on the sand with the the ripple effect is awesome, like a painting .. the mist in the background is gorgeous ... <br/>i had a similar experience, finding my laptop was totally different to my pc .. <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=829061" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">a fly in the three techniques challenge</a> .. but it was a sharpness thing as well as the colour .. i calibrated the monitor and the difference in the colours was huge .. when i processed something on the laptop before calibration and then saw it on the pc the image which looked perfect on the laptop had heaps more yellow in the same image on the pc .. anyway .. another learning experience .. <br/>hugs to you my friend .. :)xx</td>', 'hey sandy .. just came visiting and clicked on this awesome photograph .... its totally beautiful .. it looks fine on my pc but i like the darkness and the really rich orange/red of the sand .. its like a surfer has come out''v the water at the end of the day as darkness approaches .. the water on the sand with the the ripple effect is awesome, like a painting .. the mist in the background is gorgeous ... i had a similar experience, finding my laptop was totally different to my pc .. a fly in the three techniques challenge .. but it was a sharpness thing as well as the colour .. i calibrated the monitor and the difference in the colours was huge .. when i processed something on the laptop before calibration and then saw it on the pc the image which looked perfect on the laptop had heaps more yellow in the same image on the pc .. anyway .. another learning experience .. hugs to you my friend .. :)xx', '2009-11-04 18:46:55.000000', NULL, 0),
