(5747059, 815676, 100773, '<td valign="top">This deserves a post-challenge comment. I entered this FS myself, but somehow wasn''t able to vote. If I had vote, you would''ve gotten good score from me. There''s so much going on in this photo; action, light, insane colors, mystery, innocence of child playing (or whatever he does) in the water; I don''t even figure out where the heck the water is coming from! Is it rain, a fountain, what? Interesting! And the figure in the window you mentioned creeps me out; tit looks like a deleted scene from Twin Peeks. You must be satisfied with your camera for pulling that photo out of at ISO 6400! And it doesn''t surprise me a bit that it has been published on 1x; this is a true definiton on what you can achieve with one exposure. Good thing you posted that thread you did so we all could see this photo.</td>', 'This deserves a post-challenge comment. I entered this FS myself, but somehow wasn''t able to vote. If I had vote, you would''ve gotten good score from me. There''s so much going on in this photo; action, light, insane colors, mystery, innocence of child playing (or whatever he does) in the water; I don''t even figure out where the heck the water is coming from! Is it rain, a fountain, what? Interesting! And the figure in the window you mentioned creeps me out; tit looks like a deleted scene from Twin Peeks. You must be satisfied with your camera for pulling that photo out of at ISO 6400! And it doesn''t surprise me a bit that it has been published on 1x; this is a true definiton on what you can achieve with one exposure. Good thing you posted that thread you did so we all could see this photo.', '2009-11-30 16:13:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5747069, 818257, 100393, '<td valign="top">Interesting shot - I''m going to be bold and disagree with Juliet! I really like the colour treatment here and find the green grass to be particularly engaging; I like the blue hue in the sky too.<br/> <br/>The only thing that I''d perhaps take issue with is the bit of path on the left of the image - I don''t think its inclusion adds anything and it has the potential to detract.<br/> <br/>Probably would do much better in something other than a Free Study, but undervalued nonetheless IMHO.</td>', 'Interesting shot - I''m going to be bold and disagree with Juliet! I really like the colour treatment here and find the green grass to be particularly engaging; I like the blue hue in the sky too. The only thing that I''d perhaps take issue with is the bit of path on the left of the image - I don''t think its inclusion adds anything and it has the potential to detract. Probably would do much better in something other than a Free Study, but undervalued nonetheless IMHO.', '2009-11-30 16:24:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5747092, 815676, 67579, '<td valign="top">Actually I like this quite a bit, great exposure and crop!</td>', 'Actually I like this quite a bit, great exposure and crop!', '2009-11-30 16:44:38.000000', NULL, 0),
